WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:07.073
 Overall, sir,
your weapon will--

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:11.477
 Zane, Chris, congratulations.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.146
You boys have made it
into the final round

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.380
of this competition.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:15.915
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:19.085
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:25.958
That weapon is the Revolutionary
War sergeant spontoone.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.527
 Mhmm.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:29.228
 Good luck.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.897
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.799 line:7%
[heavy metal music]

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.100
ZANE: We're back in
Waxhaw, and I have

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:36.302
to make a Sergeant spontoone.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.240
I decided to use 5160
for the blade steel

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.376
because it is relatively
easy to heat treat

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:48.381
but also holds up very
well when under duress.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:51.350
My main goal is to elongate
this piece of steel that

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.152
will eventually
become the blade so

00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:54.420
that it meets the requirements.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:59.258 line:0%
Yeah, it's a slow
press, but it's OK.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.227 line:0%
CHRIS: I'm back
in my home forge.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.728
I'm ready to get started.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.330
I'm excited.

00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:06.132
I'm going to build
a Damascus billet.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.468
I'm going to try to get
as many layers as I can.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.737
I think it'll impress the
judges and hopefully hold

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:13.406
up really well on the tests.

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:14.907
I got my main billet cleaned up.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.343
I'm going to cut it and restack
it, get it to the size I need,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.180
and then I can hopefully start
getting the point shaped out.

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:25.552
 Day two, I'm going to
be working on the socket,

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.253
getting that more
fit and finished.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.889
I've also going to grind and
hopefully heat treat my blade.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:33.258
For the heat treat, I'm going to
be using this oven right here.

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:35.995
It works really well
with temperature control.

00:01:36.061 --> 00:01:38.064
I can keep my blade
exactly the temperature

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.666
that I want it for
how long I want it.

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:44.170
I'm nervous that my heat
treat is not going to go well.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.738
I could have the blade snap.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:46.973
I could have it warp.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.576
I could have it just
not harden at all.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.113
I don't hear any tinking
sound, so that's good.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.415
Tinks are usually cracks.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:59.652
And it's hard, and
I am so excited.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.422
Woo!

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.457 line:7%
That was scary.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:08.394 line:0%
CHRIS: Yesterday I got the
crossguard and the spear

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.562 line:7%
to shape.

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:13.266
The crossguard being a separate
piece is a concern of mine.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:15.067
I am going to have
to forge weld that

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.303
for structural-integrity
reasons.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:19.872 line:0%
Probably going to get into some
welding with the MIG welder

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.109 line:0%
just to reinforce everything
and, hopefully, after that,

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:26.746 line:7%
get it ready for a heat treat.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.113
 Day three is here.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.416
I plan on finishing
out my blade,

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:36.088
and then I am going to weld my
tang and my guard to my socket.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.157
That's pretty good.

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:41.394 line:0%
CHRIS: It's day for
on my spontoone build.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.697
The first thing I got to do
today is get the haft cut out

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.665
and the shape down.

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.234
I layered the wood up.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.569
Hopefully the difference
in grain structure

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:54.239
will help in strengthness
and flexibility.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:57.076
I left it sort of octagonal.

00:02:57.142 --> 00:03:00.279
I think it will give
a little better grip.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.715
Now it's time to
get my haft attached

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.184
to my spontoone spearhead.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.019
It was a hell of a build.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:07.787
I'm tired.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:08.721
I'm sore.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:12.458
I think it looks awesome.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:13.192
I cut one.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.494
I'm good.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:18.497
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.266
And I will take
your weapon, deliver

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:24.303
some thrusts and slashes
on this wild-boar carcass.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.137
Zane, you're up first.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.405
You ready for this?

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.272
 Ready as I'll ever be.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:31.744
[suspenseful music]

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:36.749
[heavy metal music]

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:54.600
 All right, Zane, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.603
First up, your tip is
really made to thrust.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.439
It punctures really deep
when I'm thrusting with it,

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:01.941
but I can move with this weapon.

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:03.175
You have a good balance here.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.710
The edge here is sharp.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:08.114
As you can see, those are
very, very deep, sharp cuts.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.317
Overall, sir, your
weapon will kill.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.185
 Thank you, Doug.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:14.620
 All right, Chris,
it's your turn.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.588
You ready?

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.189
 Yes, sir.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.860
[heavy metal music]

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.220
 All right, Chris, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:50.455
What I love about this
is when you're thrusting,

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:54.894
I can feel the weight
in front and crunch ribs

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.229
as it's penetrating.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:59.665
Overall, sir, your
weapon will kill.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:00.433
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.708
 All right, gentlemen, say
hello to my little friend.

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.847
To test the strength and
durability of your blade,

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.515
we're going to be firing
out of our air cannon

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.184
here into that wooden wall.

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:22.522
All right, Zane,
you're up first.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.825
 This thing is going to
launch my spontoone, my baby,

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:27.059
at a wall of wood.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:31.530
I'm an odd mixture between
excited and nervous right now.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:35.335
 In, 3, 2, 1, fire.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.251
All right, Zane,
nothing came apart.

00:05:52.317 --> 00:05:55.287
It still has the edge
it started out with.

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.122
All in all, good job.

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:57.890
 Thank you.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.425
CHRIS: Nice job.

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:00.827
 All right, Chris, you're up.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.168
Firing in 3, 2, 1.

00:06:10.235 --> 00:06:10.903
Fire.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.209
CHRIS: Wow.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.477
 Good job, Chris.

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:25.718
OK, your weapon went right
in between those boards,

00:06:25.784 --> 00:06:28.988
so it actually took all the
impact up here on these lugs.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.890
Everything's still
straight, still sharp.

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:34.192
I really like that
pattern you got on there.

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:34.926
Nicely done.

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:35.761
 Thank you.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:38.063
 That is nice.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:42.135
[suspenseful music]

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:45.938
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the sharpness test,

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.807
the redcoat stab and slice.

00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:54.246
To test the sharpness of your
edge, I will take your weapon

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:57.516
and slash stab
across this redcoat.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.450
Zane, you're up first.

00:06:58.517 --> 00:06:59.419
Let's do it.

00:07:09.094 --> 00:07:13.065
[heavy metal music]

00:07:28.747 --> 00:07:31.617
All right, Zane,
your edges are sharp.

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.552
On the swing of
that, it does cut.

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:37.522
But what I do find
here is a little bit

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:39.024
of a glinting at your tip.

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.059
It catches on my nails.

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:43.662
It rolled a little bit
right there at your tip.

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:46.732
But otherwise, sir, it will cut.

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:48.534
 Thank you.

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:49.769
 All right, Chris, your turn.

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.937
 Let's do this.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:55.874
Things have actually been
really even between Zane and I.

00:07:55.941 --> 00:08:01.146
I just hope my spontoone,
it's strong and sharp enough.

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:02.547
This is it.

00:08:02.581 --> 00:08:06.752
[suspenseful music]

00:08:07.552 --> 00:08:11.724
[heavy metal music]

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:36.582
 All right, Chris, this is
a very razor-sharp blade.

00:08:36.648 --> 00:08:40.453
Every slash and
thrust was a deep cut.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:43.822
I do not see any
damage to your edge.

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:48.059
Overall, sir, this
weapon will cut.

00:08:48.126 --> 00:08:49.961
 Thank you.

00:08:49.995 --> 00:08:52.465
 Zane, Chris, you guys
have done fantastic work

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:54.266
on these finale weapons,
but there can only

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.634
be one "Forged in
Fire" champion,

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:58.437
and the judges have made
their final decision.

00:08:58.503 --> 00:09:04.310
And that "Forged in
Fire" champion is Chris.

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.478
Congratulations.

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:07.312
You are the new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:07.379 --> 00:09:08.714
 Congratulations, man.

00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:10.249
 Zane, unfortunately
your weapon

00:09:10.315 --> 00:09:14.053
took some damage during the
sharpness test which affected

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.287
the efficacy of your cuts.

00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:17.657
For that reason, I'd like to
invite you to shake my hand,

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:20.626
shake your judges' hands, and
then please leave the forge.

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:21.627
Came on, my friend.

00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:22.695
 --to meet you guys.

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:23.762
 Good job, brother.

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:26.131
 I did not win, but that's OK.

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:27.166
 It's a great weapon.

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:28.801
 I came here to
prove that I was

00:09:28.867 --> 00:09:31.237
able to compete with
some of the big dogs,

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.171
and I think I made my point.

00:09:33.238 --> 00:09:35.908
I hope that I'll be able to
keep improving upon my craft

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:38.277
and just get better and better.

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:40.813
 Chris, you crafted
a better weapon

00:09:40.879 --> 00:09:42.981
that held up through the tests.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:43.882
Congratulations.

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:45.384 line:0%
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:47.653 line:0%
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:48.721 line:7%
Good job, brother.

00:09:48.788 --> 00:09:49.521
Come over here and
shake our heads.

00:09:49.588 --> 00:09:50.755
 Absolutely.

00:09:50.822 --> 00:09:52.758
CHRIS: I just became
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:54.025
[laughs] That's crazy.

00:09:54.092 --> 00:09:56.795
I'm, like, turning
inside out right now.

00:09:56.861 --> 00:09:58.196
I got the bragging rights, man.

00:09:58.263 --> 00:10:02.134
I can just keep moving ahead,
keep doing what I'm doing.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:05.671
[heavy metal music]

